{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1023616-hurt-locker-help-with-fighting-styles-tags","id":1023616,"title":"[Hurt Locker] Help with Fighting Styles Tags","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-29T00:52:39-08:00","id":1023616,"title":"[Hurt Locker] Help with Fighting Styles Tags","content":"I'm trying to wrap my head around concepts of Styles Tags. I understand that characters can 'swipe' some maneuvers in his Style 'tree' for others - or can buy other maneuvers as 1 dot Merits. I just cannot grasp <i>when</i> character do it. I understand that some sum of 'hierarchical' Style dots are in order - I just do not understand how this goes. I would be greatful for any help with this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T07:23:26-08:00","id":1023749,"title":"","content":"For the most part, Styles work as before.<br /> <br /> If you want to swipe a manouver from one style a another (if they share appropiate tags) you just need to have the same number of pre-requisite merits.<br /> <br /> For example, I made a custom Hung Gar Style. I made 3 new merits for the first three levels, and then used the 4th and 5th merits from Martial Arts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T13:08:53-08:00","id":1024879,"title":"","content":"I think this is how it works. If I'm wrong, please correct me.<br /> Merits with Style Tags can be used as prerequisites to buy maneuvers in a Style Chain with the same Style Tag. Let's take the Martial Arts Style in Hurt Locker and break it down into just its parts and Prerequisites. For the purposes of this explanation, I'll be ignoring the alternate maneuver rules. Treating each maneuver in the Martial Arts Merit as its own Merit, it looks kind of like something like this:<br /> Leg Kick (\u2022) - Prerequisites: Resolve \u2022\u2022\u2022, Dexterity \u2022\u2022\u2022, Athletics \u2022\u2022, Brawl \u2022\u2022<br /> Cutting Elbow (\u2022) - Prerequisites: Leg Kick<br /> Trapping (\u2022) - Prerequisites: Cutting Elbow<br /> Inch Force (\u2022) - Prerequisites: Trapping<br /> High Momentum Strike (\u2022) - Prerequisites: Inch Force<br /> <br /> Using the new Style Tag rules, it now looks like this:<br /> Leg Kick (\u2022) (Striking) - Prerequisites: Resolve \u2022\u2022\u2022, Dexterity \u2022\u2022\u2022, Athletics \u2022\u2022, Brawl \u2022\u2022<br /> Cutting Elbow (\u2022) (Striking) - Prerequisites: Leg Kick OR Prerequisites: Resolve \u2022\u2022\u2022, Dexterity \u2022\u2022\u2022, Athletics \u2022\u2022, Brawl \u2022\u2022 and at least two Dots in Merits with the (Striking) Tag.<br /> Trapping (\u2022) (Striking) - Prerequisites: Cutting Elbow OR Prerequisites: Resolve \u2022\u2022\u2022, Dexterity \u2022\u2022\u2022, Athletics \u2022\u2022, Brawl \u2022\u2022 and at least three Dots in Merits with the (Striking) Tag.<br /> Inch Force (\u2022) (Striking) - Prerequisites: Trapping OR Prerequisites: Resolve \u2022\u2022\u2022, Dexterity \u2022\u2022\u2022, Athletics \u2022\u2022, Brawl \u2022\u2022 and at least four Dots in Merits with the (Striking) Tag.<br /> High Momentum Strike (\u2022) (Striking) - Prerequisites: Inch Force (\u2022) OR Prerequisites: Resolve \u2022\u2022\u2022, Dexterity \u2022\u2022\u2022, Athletics \u2022\u2022, Brawl \u2022\u2022 and at least five Dots in Merits with the (Striking) Tag.<br /> <br /> For example, To be eligible to learn Trapping, a character with Resolve \u2022\u2022\u2022, Dexterity \u2022\u2022\u2022, Athletics \u2022\u2022, Brawl \u2022\u2022 can<br /> -Learn the Leg Kick and Cutting Elbow maneuvers in the Martial Arts Style Merit (the normal rules)<br /> -Learn Leg Kick and and a Two-Dot Merit with the (Striking) Tag like Iron Chin \u2022\u2022<br /> -Learn a Three-Dot Merit with the (Striking) Tag like Ground and Pound.<br /> Or whatever other combination gives you three Dots in Merits with (Striking)<br /> <br /> I am not sure how this works when we collapse it back. If something has Martial Arts \u2022\u2022 as a Prerequisite, is that now &quot;Any two maneuvers from the Martial Arts Merit&quot;?<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that if a maneuver in a Style Merit has a maneuver as an additional prerequisite, you can't ignore it through Style Tags. Also, Maneuvers in Styles based on certain weapons still require those weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8064,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8064-mp122984","user":"mp122984","date":". 12-31-2016, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8064-mp122984","name":"mp122984","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T14:55:02-08:00","id":1024911,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8064-mp122984\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8064\" data-vbnamecard=\"8064\">mp122984</a> has it right. Basically, with the Style Tag rules, Maneuvers from any Fighting Style can be bought <i>a la carte</i> for 1 experience each, as long as you have a total number of dots equal to one less than the level of the Maneuver in Fighting Merits with the same tag. So, for example, let's say you want Trained Gouge (Kino Mutai \u2022\u2022\u2022), but you don't care about the first two dots of the style. You could instead buy the first two dots of Berserker, since they both have the Enraged Tag. And then, you could pick up Knocking the Wind Out (Street Fighting \u2022\u2022) while you're at it without having to buy the first dots, since Kino Mutai has the Street Tag and you have one dot of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T15:34:13-08:00","id":1024923,"title":"","content":"Is it one less? Page 45 says, &quot;The character needs to first possess as many Merit dots in same Style Tag as the rank (in Fighting Style progression) of the unorthodox or extra maneuver she wishes to learn.&quot; And the example on page 46 says &quot;Musa\u2019s four dots of Striking Merits allow him to learn anything up to The Hand as Weapon without methodically advancing up the style.&quot; where The Hand as Weapon is a Four-Dot Maneuver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8064-mp122984","name":"mp122984","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T16:16:34-08:00","id":1024936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mp122984</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1023616-hurt-locker-help-with-fighting-styles-tags?p=1024923#post1024923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it one less? Page 45 says, &amp;quot;The character needs to first possess as many Merit dots in same Style Tag as the rank (in Fighting Style progression) of the unorthodox or extra maneuver she wishes to learn.&amp;quot; And the example on page 46 says &amp;quot;Musa\u2019s four dots of Striking Merits allow him to learn anything up to The Hand as Weapon without methodically advancing up the style.&amp;quot; where The Hand as Weapon is a Four-Dot Maneuver.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, weird. I guess that is the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T04:51:06-08:00","id":1025853,"title":"","content":"Kinda wish there was a way to add a Tag to one specific manuever. There is &quot;transfer manuever&quot;, but surprisingly enough I would rather turn something into Movement (Strong) to make middle dots of Strength Performance more to my liking, or slap Heavy Melee on Manic Brutality and weaponize random objects using their new glorious damage rating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}